# 26. Features that will make your app stand out

I would add these features even if competing apps don't offer them in the same way:

1. Modular editing workspace: Users can customize their own editing interface.
2. Desktop-style timeline on mobile: Support landscape mode, mouse, keyboard and stylus.
3. AI editing copilot: Users can describe an edit in natural language and the AI creates a proposed timeline.
4. Smart performance mode: Automatically adjusts preview quality based on device performance.
5. Professional color workflow: Include LUTs, scopes, curves and color management.
6. One-tap social export: Automatically creates versions for different platforms.
7. Custom plugin system: Allow developers to create additional effects and transitions.
8. Offline-first editing: Core editing should work without internet.
9. Non-destructive editing: Preserve original media and store editing instructions separately.
10. Professional project interchange: Allow users to move projects between compatible editing software.

## 27. Important mobile performance requirements

A professional Android editor has to account for mobile hardware limitations.

- Dynamic preview resolution: Full, half, quarter and eighth resolution.
- GPU-accelerated effects.
- Background thumbnail generation.
- Intelligent memory management.
- Automatic proxy generation.
- Frame caching.
- Hardware codec detection.
- Adaptive export quality.
- Battery and temperature monitoring.
- Background rendering with recovery.
- Large-project memory management.
- Device-specific performance profiles.

For example, an entry-level phone should be able to edit a complex project using proxies, even if it cannot play the original 4K footage with every effect in real time.

My recommendation: Aim for professional editing capabilities, but don't promise desktop DaVinci Resolve performance on Android. Resolve combines editing, Fusion, color grading and Fairlight in separate professional workspaces; that's a useful architectural model for your application.&#x20;

